{
    "background_story": "Duckling was a happy-go-lucky duck who lived in a cozy pond with his feathered friends. However, one day he began to feel sluggish and lethargic. His feathers lost their luster, and he developed an unusual growth on his beak. The other ducks avoided him, fearing the unknown condition. A wise old goose, who had seen many ailments in her years, diagnosed Duckling with costiasis, a parasitic infection common in waterfowl. She taught him how to treat the condition with a special diet and herbal remedies. With time and care, Duckling recovered, and his feathers regained their former glory. Grateful for his second chance, he became an advocate for waterfowl health, educating his fellow ducks on the importance of maintaining a clean and healthy environment.",
